        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T17:45:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to be clear, are *we* defining CUSTOM heap this way, or is something external (d3d12 or driver or chromium?) define it this way?\n\nIn general I\u0027m a bit confused about the high level logic here so a high level comment would be helpful. For example why do we branch on `isUMA` instead of some driver-reported info for this specific heap from `heapProperties`? `isUMA` seems possibly too broad. (Maybe this is the same as Corentin\u0027s comment.)",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c224ca2_4c4b60ee",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T22:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe that https://microsoft.github.io/DirectX-Specs/d3d/D3D12GPUUploadHeaps.html explains it. I\u0027m just following the specification for READBACK/UPLOAD/DEFAULT and ignoring GPU_UPLOAD. I\u0027ll add a table in the comments and cite that link.",
      "parentUuid": "174523d0_53536b88",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2427ed87_2e9bf453",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000268
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-03T22:45:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@enrico.galli@intel.com GPU upload heaps are a special case that WebNN cannot export. The `ID3D12Device::GetCustomHeapProperties` API used by WebNN simply maps READBACK, UPLOAD, and DEFAULT heap types to their corresponding custom heap properties (i.e., for UMA systems, these properties are still predefined by D3D). See `ID3D12Device::GetCustomHeapProperties` [1] for the documented mappings.\n\n[1] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/nf-d3d12-id3d12device-getcustomheapproperties(uint_d3d12_heap_type)",
      "parentUuid": "4c224ca2_4c4b60ee",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00cea95c_37ec2c2b",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-05T06:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added a link to the `GetCustomHeapProperties` MSDN page in mapping function.",
      "parentUuid": "2427ed87_2e9bf453",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d58f4523_9bbd5582",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-05T06:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Just to be clear, are we defining CUSTOM heap this way, or is something external (d3d12 or driver or chromium?) define it this way?\n\nA little bit of both. We are using the definitions from `ID3D12Device::GetCustomHeapProperties(UINT,D3D12_HEAP_TYPE)` plus the fact that in UMA systems, the GPU always has access to the buffers.\n\n\u003e In general I\u0027m a bit confused about the high level logic here so a high level comment would be helpful. For example why do we branch on isUMA instead of some driver-reported info for this specific heap from heapProperties? isUMA seems possibly too broad. (Maybe this is the same as Corentin\u0027s comment.)\n\nUnfortunately, we need to know if we are running in a UMA system to know if we can give the `DEFAULT`-like usages to `UPLOAD`/`READBACK`-equivalent `heapProperties`. For example, a heap in `L0` (system ram) and `WRITE_BACK` could either be `READBACK`-equivalent (NUMA system), `READBACK` + `DEFAULT` (non-cache coherent UMA), or `READBACK` + `UPLOAD` + `DEFAULT` (ccUMA).",
      "parentUuid": "3dac9435_a7208efe",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
