        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-01T12:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If possible, I\u0027d rather avoid adding MapWrite here because there is no way for Dawn to ensure that the application won\u0027t read the mapped memory, which would be insanely slow in this mode.",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e99cdb40_edb4f4a2",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T22:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that L0 + WRITE_COMBINE is equivalent to UPLOAD heaps on non ccUMA architectures. We use [d3d12_device_-\u003eGetCustomHeapProperties(0, D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_UPLOAD)](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/d3d_image_backing_factory.cc;l\u003d824;drc\u003d9b4c9ad003587ffb6878dd7e3aa7f83c07d7747d) in shared image. That said, we don\u0027t currently have a use-case for MapAsync from WebGPU. WebNN can always WriteTensor/ReadTensor to/from these resources (even if it would be slow).",
      "parentUuid": "d3a21d69_0c284c55",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
